INT. CHEESE-AGING CAVE - NIGHT

Limestone walls, wooden racks of wheels, a fog of ammonia and mold. A single bulb swings on a cord.

MARISOL FUENTES (30s, climbing harness, headlamp) lowers herself off a ladder while CASPIAN DUBOIS (40s, careful hands, white coat stolen from a cheesemonger) checks a humidity gauge and IGGY BRANNIGAN (20s, nervous, duffel bag) props open the freight door with a wheel of Gruyere. SUNITA RAO (50s, retired locksmith, reading glasses on a chain) kneels at a steel cabinet at the back, picks in hand.

MARISOL
Eleven minutes. That's the guard's loop.

CASPIAN
Nine. I counted.

IGGY
It smells like feet in here.

SUNITA
It smells like money. Hush.

The cabinet clicks. Sunita pulls the door. Inside, velvet-lined shelves cradle a row of small glass jars. Marisol reaches in.

MARISOL
Starter cultures.

CASPIAN
Four hundred years old. Worth more than gold.

IGGY
It's cheese mold.

SUNITA
It's the cheese mold.

Iggy lifts a jar. Caspian takes the next one. Marisol begins loading the duffel. Everything is calm, almost gentle, like four people in a pantry.

A flashlight beam sweeps across the entrance.

MADAME ELOISE THIBAULT (70s, nightgown, wellington boots, a shotgun held like an umbrella) steps through the freight door. She does not look surprised.

MADAME THIBAULT
Put them back.

IGGY
We were just--

MARISOL
Madame, we can explain.

CASPIAN
Don't explain.

SUNITA
She's holding a shotgun, Caspian, explain something.

MADAME THIBAULT
Put them back. Every one. Then you may leave.

The four of them glance at each other. Marisol sets the duffel down. Caspian nudges a jar back with one finger. Iggy sobs quietly. Sunita sighs and replaces the cabinet door.

MADAME THIBAULT (CONT'D)
The key is in the left pocket of my robe. It always was.

Sunita peers at her.

SUNITA
You left it unlocked.

MADAME THIBAULT
I left it for the mice. You, I did not expect.
